 "text": "Hey, good to have you here. How are you? Most bikes have a sticker under the seat tube that says the height. If you can't find one, hold the seat post midway under the wheel. Most people find 9 out of 10 bikes are too high at the factory. If yours feels good, leave it. It' okay. Then lower it bit, until it feels right. Then raise it with a shorter tube and a spacer or two fewer. Whichever feels good. Most people sit slightly forward, so it' worth checking that you can still see the traffic while you're up there.",
